WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
[Kelly] I've got Blake Shelton with me

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:04.801
and in New York via
Skype is Cynthia Nixon!

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:07.130
(cheering and applause)

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:10.115
Blake, is it fair to say that
you shared a drink or maybe 13

00:00:10.115 --> 00:00:11.967
with like everyone in country music?

00:00:11.967 --> 00:00:12.800
[Blake] Yes.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:13.633
- Okay.

00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:14.466
- Yes.

00:00:14.466 --> 00:00:15.299
- So, just wanted to make sure.

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:16.966
Well there's one drink
Blake may have skipped.

00:00:16.966 --> 00:00:19.240
I was talking with Little Big Town the

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.726
other day and they had this to say:

00:00:21.726 --> 00:00:23.507
Jimmy, wine beer whiskey,

00:00:23.507 --> 00:00:25.244
Thomas Rhett,

00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:28.865
University of Alabama
football coach, Nick Saban.

00:00:28.865 --> 00:00:31.810
And what the hell, we'll just keep Shelton

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:33.407
'cause people like him here.

00:00:33.407 --> 00:00:36.120
[Thomas] and I would say wine with Blake

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.190
because that would be
the least obvious choice

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:39.770
and I think it would be hilarious

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:42.271
trying to have a refined
wine conversation.

00:00:42.271 --> 00:00:45.202
(laughter)

00:00:45.202 --> 00:00:48.360
- That's awesome.
- The paper cuts would be fun.

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.640
- I love that, I realized they were right.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.070
So I need to drink wine with
Blake, which brings us here.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.470
Joining us now is the
founder of SommSelect,

00:00:57.470 --> 00:01:00.530
and one of 300 masters
sommeliers in the world.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:03.304
Please welcome in Ian Cauble.

00:01:03.304 --> 00:01:04.904
What's up Ian?

00:01:04.904 --> 00:01:07.190
[Ian] What's up everybody,
thanks for having me.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:08.440
- Nice to see you again.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:11.326
So how much experience,
Ian, do you have teaching

00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:15.120
beer, whiskey, and, vodka
drinking country boys about wine?

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.170
- Very little, actually,

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:19.190
but I think Blake's a pro and
he's a great test subject.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.057
So, I think he'll be successful.

00:01:21.057 --> 00:01:23.290
- Blake and I have wine here,

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:25.978
and Cynthia has the
same wines in New York.

00:01:25.978 --> 00:01:28.495
Are you all set, Cynthia?

00:01:28.495 --> 00:01:30.150
[Cynthia] I am, I definitely am.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.190
- All right. All right.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.895
Well what will we be tasting, Ian?

00:01:32.895 --> 00:01:35.870
- So today we're focused on
Burgundy, my favorite region

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:37.566
of the world, and this
is pretty much mecca

00:01:37.566 --> 00:01:39.540
for great Pinot Noir du Chardonnay.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.530
So let's start with this first wine.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:44.268
So we have a John Mark
PO premiere Cru coming

00:01:44.268 --> 00:01:47.380
from Chassagne Montrachet,
very famous village.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.640
This is kind of like a fairy
tale for people who love wine.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:51.920
So let's go ahead and

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:53.996
smell the first wine first and foremost

00:01:53.996 --> 00:01:58.847
let's go ahead and grab the--nice
glasses by the way, Kelly.

00:01:58.847 --> 00:01:59.680
- Hey, I don't know if you know

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.035
but we won an Emmy, so
we're upping our game.

00:02:03.035 --> 00:02:04.030
- Fancy.

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.960
So first and foremost, let's
go ahead and grab the wine

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.340
by the stem.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.350
You don't want to get the
wine warm with your hand.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.380
If you're at a party and
you're holding the glass

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:14.780
by the stem or by the
bulb you're basically

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.460
gonna warm your glass pretty quickly.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:17.444
Nice work, Cynthia.

00:02:17.444 --> 00:02:19.070
- Yeah, Blake is looking good.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.892
- So lets go ahead and
put the glass on the table

00:02:21.892 --> 00:02:24.312
- You're not getting any,
if you hold your glass

00:02:24.312 --> 00:02:26.740
but like this at a party
cause people will know-

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:27.840
- You're not getting any! (laughing)

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.132
- Yeah, you know what I
mean? It's like, loser!

00:02:30.132 --> 00:02:32.830
(all laughing)

00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:34.480
You're gonna want to
put the base of the stem

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.310
right here, at the base of
your nose here. A little bit.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.760
What are you smelling, Blake?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.351
- Why, what do you mean?

00:02:43.351 --> 00:02:46.370
(audience and Kelly laughing)

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.880
- Are you smelling any white or peaches?

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:51.763
- Oh yeah it is kinda fruit, right? Fruit?

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:53.890
- Can I taste it?

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:54.723
- Yeah, lets taste it.

00:02:54.723 --> 00:02:55.770
- Okay!

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:57.110
- We'll taste about a half ounce

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:58.920
and then I want you to
swirl it around your palette

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.820
for about five or six seconds
and expose all your taste buds

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.873
to it, swallow it without your nose.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.370
You should be getting a
lot of information going

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.349
to your brain about all
the different fruits.

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:15.500
- Oh! It's like collecting in my cheeks

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.439
and the insides of my cheeks.

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:18.730
It's nice, like a little party.

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.840
- Exactly and you're
getting a lot of acidity

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.601
and freshness and this minerality.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.980
Is anybody tasting a lot of
this like mineral component?

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.732
Almost like like oyster shell maybe?

00:03:27.732 --> 00:03:29.040
- That's what I was gonna
say yeah, mineral component.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.150
That's what I was going to.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:31.210
I was going to leave with that.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.990
It's weird that you did
first, but I'll just

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.809
let you talk about it.

00:03:34.809 --> 00:03:36.710
- So this region used to exist

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.190
under a shallow ocean for
about 200 million years.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:42.048
So all of the seashells
decompose creating limestone.

00:03:42.048 --> 00:03:43.240
So what you're tasting

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:47.000
on the pallet is actually 185
million years in the making.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.210
If that makes it taste any better.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:49.297
- Bad snails.

00:03:49.297 --> 00:03:52.160
- (laughing)

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:52.993
- What in the hell?

00:03:52.993 --> 00:03:55.290
- Oh my gosh, that's actually
awesome that information!

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.078
- We can go back to bourbon
if you want Blake, It's fine.

00:03:58.078 --> 00:03:59.740
- Oh, I like bourbon too.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.030
I like--I like this.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.240
- I like this too.

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:03.950
- This is actually the
first thing I've done

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.375
on this show, that's worth a crap.

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:08.428
Drinking. Drinking, finally.

00:04:08.428 --> 00:04:09.481
(laughing)

00:04:09.481 --> 00:04:10.863
- This next one is a pinot

00:04:10.863 --> 00:04:12.668
one and Ian, you know that's my favorite.

00:04:12.668 --> 00:04:14.070
- I do know that.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:16.690
So this is coming from the
next village, just south.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:20.410
This is called Santana coming
from a 120 year old vine.

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:22.720
So you can imagine that these great

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:25.400
vines have roots that are
going down almost as far

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:26.763
as a 10 story building.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.553
What does everyone smell?

00:04:28.553 --> 00:04:29.386
- Oh!

00:04:31.381 --> 00:04:33.210
- This is going to sound
weird, but like leather.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.324
I don't know why I don't--

00:04:34.324 --> 00:04:37.094
- You know, I totally agree with you.

00:04:37.094 --> 00:04:39.890
It smells like leather.

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.650
- Like, like aged leather,
like a really nice leather

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.870
jacket that I want to drink.

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:46.385
- He's known for having more earthy tones

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:48.270
and so you're getting it, for me,

00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:49.870
you're getting this strawberry blossom

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.080
almost strawberry
preserves, but there's a lot

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.134
of secondary characters
of like leather mushroom

00:04:54.134 --> 00:04:57.810
a little bit of like crushed rocks accents

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.924
of a little bit of baking
spices of vanilla from--

00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:01.573
- Yea, because I was going to say that too

00:05:01.573 --> 00:05:03.060
but I'll let you say it first though.

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:03.990
That was cool.

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:04.823
- That's my favorite.

00:05:04.823 --> 00:05:06.010
- And this is a really young wine

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.745
and this wine is truly
gonna reach its peak

00:05:07.745 --> 00:05:09.636
in about 10 to 15 years.

00:05:09.636 --> 00:05:11.460
- I just want to give a shout

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:12.680
out cause I know that Christine

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.260
and our audience, I
noticed she had some wine.

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:15.630
She sippin wine with us today y'all.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.680
Get it Christina! Yes!

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.302
Okay. Well, let's try vodka
cause I wanted to try it.

00:05:21.302 --> 00:05:22.374
- Yes.

00:05:22.374 --> 00:05:24.120
- This is Blake's vodka.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.140
Everybody's got some, we've
got them a little tiny

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:29.223
little cute, adorable
little mini solo cups.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:33.020
So let's smell it first.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:34.350
Here we go.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.170
What notes do you get,
Ian, from Blake's vodka?

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.330
- Well, I thought y'all might
of poured water in there.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.163
- No!

00:05:40.163 --> 00:05:40.996
- That's real.

00:05:40.996 --> 00:05:42.618
- I am authentic, bro.

00:05:42.618 --> 00:05:45.320
- We're drinking the real deal.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.269
- Okay, wait. Let's taste--

00:05:46.269 --> 00:05:48.030
- You know what? I'll say this.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.629
The best vodkas in the
world don't have much aroma.

00:05:50.629 --> 00:05:52.389
The greatest vodkas are very clean

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:55.020
and I was actually sipping
on this before the show

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:56.469
and it's really good. It's very elegant.

00:05:56.469 --> 00:05:59.397
- (laughing) My man!

00:05:59.397 --> 00:06:01.623
You know exactly what
you're talking about.

00:06:03.366 --> 00:06:06.480
- It's no joke, this is really
good. It's really smooth.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.250
And you know, good job.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.463
- Okay, cheers.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.410
- I'm going to send you
a case of it Cynthia.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:15.363
- Please do.

00:06:15.363 --> 00:06:16.196
- I haven't had a shot in a while.

00:06:16.196 --> 00:06:17.695
- Did she really do it?

00:06:17.695 --> 00:06:18.528
- Yes!

00:06:18.528 --> 00:06:19.610
- Oh my god.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.180
You have to fill more of these today?

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.103
- It's just one shot, mama's fine.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:29.580
I smell hints of regret twenties

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.144
and someone holding my hair.

00:06:31.144 --> 00:06:32.800
- (laughing)

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:33.633
- That's what I'm tasting

00:06:33.633 --> 00:06:36.116
as well, poor decisions;
that's what I smell.

00:06:36.116 --> 00:06:37.334
That's what I taste.

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:41.075
Congrats Blake, Master Somm
has approved your vodka.

00:06:41.075 --> 00:06:44.470
That's amazing.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:45.303
- Thank you!

00:06:45.303 --> 00:06:48.068
